⍝ OperPower.tc
⍝ ----------------------------------

⍝@ test3.

      PLUS  ← { ⍺ + ⍵ }
      EQUIV ← { ⍺ ≡ ⍵ }
      EQUAL ← { ⍺ = ⍵ }

      ⍝ numeric RO
      ⍝
      2 (+ ⍣ 40) 5
85

      ⍝ numeric RO w/o parentheses (GNU APL extension)
      ⍝
      2 + ⍣ 40 5
85

      ⍝ numeric RO defined function LO
      ⍝
      2 (PLUS ⍣ 40) 5
85

      ⍝ numeric RO defined function LO w/o parentheses
      ⍝
      2 PLUS ⍣ 40 5
85

      ⍝ primitive RO
      ⍝
      ({2+⍵÷2}⍣≡) 9
4
      ({2+⍵÷2}⍣=) 9
4

      ⍝ defined RO
      ⍝
      ({2+⍵÷2}⍣EQUIV) 9
4
      ({2+⍵÷2}⍣EQUAL) 9
4

      ⍝ inverse (integer N < 0)
      ⍝
      2 (+ ⍣ 40) 5
85
      2 (+ ⍣ ¯40) 85
5

      2 (- ⍣ ¯40) 5
5
      2 (- ⍣ ¯40) 5
5

      ⍝ Dyalog examples (MasterinDyalogAPL.pdf)
      ⍝

      ⍝ 8.3 - Left Argument (All Forms) p. 417
      3(×⍣4)2
162

      ⍝ Spe-3.1 p. 427
      ⎕RL ← 1
      Stupid ← {? ⍺ + ⍵ ⊣ ⎕←'⍺=',(⍕⍺),' ⍵=',⍕⍵}
      10 (Stupid ⍣ <) 20
⍺=10 ⍵=20
12

      ⍝ dito w/o parentheses
      ⎕RL ← 1
      10 Stupid ⍣ < 20
⍺=10 ⍵=20
12

      ⍝ https://aplwiki.com/wiki/Strand_notation
      ⍝
      2 (×⍣3) 2
16

      2×⍣3 ⊢2
16

      ⍝ regression
      ⍝
      {1+÷⍵}⍣2 ⊢ 2
1.666666667

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs26 #5): same bug as Rank.tc's ⍤
      ⍝ case, but in fix_POWER_syntax() for ⍣ -- pos_LO = pos_POWER - 1
      ⍝ grabbed only the trailing operator (/), not the whole derived
      ⍝ function +/, so +/⍣2 B parenthesized itself as +(/⍣2) B instead
      ⍝ of (+/)⍣2 B -- reported as SYNTAX ERROR.
      ⍝
      +/⍣2⊢1 2 3
6
      (+/)⍣2⊢1 2 3
6

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs31 #21): fix_POWER_syntax()'s
      ⍝ LO_has_axis exception (Bugs30 #20) only fired for a LITERAL N --
      ⍝ the two non-literal-N shortcuts just above it (skip an already-
      ⍝ parenthesized N, and bail out entirely when N isn't a literal at
      ⍝ all) both ran first, so LO[axis]⍣N never reached the exception
      ⍝ whenever N was a variable or itself parenthesized, unlike the ⍤
      ⍝ analogue (fix_RANK_syntax()), which was already axis-aware for
      ⍝ every shape of its right operand.
      ⍝
      M←2 3⍴⍳6 ⋄ N←2

      (⌽[1]⍣3)M
4 5 6
1 2 3

      (⌽[1]⍣N)M
1 2 3
4 5 6

      (⌽[1]⍣(N))M
1 2 3
4 5 6

      (⌽[1]⍣(2))M
1 2 3
4 5 6

      ⍝ control: the ⍤ analogue already worked (Bugs30 #21), and still
      ⍝ does -- included here only to confirm the fix above didn't
      ⍝ regress it (⍤ is RANK, not repetition, so the printed value
      ⍝ itself isn't meant to match the ⍣ cases above)
      ⍝
      ⌽[1]⍤N ⊢M
4 5 6
1 2 3

      )ERASE M N

      )CHECK BRIEF

      ⍝ ==================================

